<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1cca78539255b7294af8498f5e21f9dd52bc8040" commit="25ed526e8d2f10ab817de513c0f0dc9ae42d15aa" commit_message="login: Implement prioritization of Androind container  When chrome sends the PrioritizeArcInstance D-Bus message, reset the Android cpu.shares to the default value so that Android processes have equal access to cpu resources.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:56555 TEST=cat cpu.shares before and after starting Android after login.  Change-Id: I1cca78539255b7294af8498f5e21f9dd52bc8040 Signed-off-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/383983 Reviewed-by: Yusuke Sato &lt;yusukes@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="383983" owner_email="dgreid@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/83/383983/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2c391abc665e4f8d98c17a06701d80b7b54e4d49" commit="2fbf8f051f612402d67949ebf0460502aa447c86" commit_message="login: ui.conf - Place ui processes in a cpu cgroup  This moves all of the Chrome processes to the /ui cpu cgroup.  Moving these processes to a cgroup at a parallel level to Android allows for setting relative priority between Chrome and Android by setting the relative cpu.shares of each cgroup.  Chrome renderers will still be put in the top level and will be unaffected by this change, however a Chrome change will move them down to be children of Chrome so they can be boosted/cut as well.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:56243 TEST=check system responsiveness after login  Signed-off-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: I2c391abc665e4f8d98c17a06701d80b7b54e4d49 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/380327 Reviewed-by: David Reveman &lt;reveman@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="380327" owner_email="dgreid@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/27/380327/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If0bb44ff1df5f613c8fbec22a2c6ce7a2d048add" commit="1d9fb6f2430757d96d86f735d3c32c00a95199d1" commit_message="login: ui.conf - Limit Android cpu usage during login  Limit the amount of cpu that Android processes can use during Chrome login.  Use the cpu cgroup to achieve this.  The limit is removed by login_manager when Chrome indicates that Android needs priority with the &quot;PrioritizeArcInstance&quot; D-Bus message.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:56555 TEST=Check Android's cpu.shares value before and after starting the play store app.  Change-Id: If0bb44ff1df5f613c8fbec22a2c6ce7a2d048add Signed-off-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/383984 Reviewed-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="383984" owner_email="dgreid@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/84/383984/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.8" change_id="Id627b3b6ae8f2718911da091bb08034dccbdef48" commit="0e3ced99b78f96af2755c02fdfac9ec80d20af60" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/exynos: remove KDS sync  We haven't been using it for a while since it was replaced with implicit fence based sync and we will never use it again.  BUG=598126 TEST=build and install kernel 3.8, run webgl aquarium  Change-Id: Id627b3b6ae8f2718911da091bb08034dccbdef48 Signed-off-by: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/384633 Reviewed-by: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="384633" owner_email="dbehr@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/33/384633/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie389c11e26aa617189e610295fcc01e3e87c9b24" commit="f48419f1e4bb36abb467268d123d198af4e3dced" commit_message="Gale drivers: Add qup3 i2c changes  1.Added the support for changing the i2c duty cycle settings. Default duty-cycle for qup3 i2c is set to 30/70.  2.Enabled the qup3 i2c controller clock frequency setting to 19.05 Mhz.  3.Added the support for noise reject feature for qup3 i2c controller. Default value noise-rej-sda and noise-rej-scl is set to 1.  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:56399 TEST=System boot  Change-Id: Ie389c11e26aa617189e610295fcc01e3e87c9b24 Signed-off-by: Jaiganesh Narayanan &lt;njaigane@codeaurora.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/384295 Commit-Ready: Kan Yan &lt;kyan@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Kan Yan &lt;kyan@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Kan Yan &lt;kyan@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="384295" owner_email="njaigane@codeaurora.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" ref="refs/changes/95/384295/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I1645a5ff2ce5867f907a6fbdd9f5e4d0052f3f4e" commit="6f3f68055a01bb6740ebd3bd577511d5592110e1" commit_message="UPSTREAM: i2c: designware: save the preset value of DW_IC_SDA_HOLD  There are several ways to set the SDA hold time for i2c controller, including: Device Tree, built-in device properties and ACPI. However, if the SDA hold time is not specified by above method, we should read the value, where it is preset by firmware, and save it to sda_hold_time. This is needed because when i2c controller enters runtime suspend, the DW_IC_SDA_HOLD value will be reset to chipset default value. And during runtime resume, i2c_dw_init will be called to reconfigure i2c controller. If sda_hold_time is zero, the chipset default hold time will be used, that will be too short for some platforms. Therefore, to have a better tolerance, the DW_IC_SDA_HOLD value should be kept by sda_hold_time.  Signed-off-by: Zhuo-hao Lee &lt;zhuo-hao.lee@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Andy Shevchenko &lt;andriy.shevchenko@linux.intel.com&gt; Acked-by: Jarkko Nikula &lt;jarkko.nikula@linux.intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Wolfram Sang &lt;wsa@the-dreams.de&gt; (cherry picked from commit 664d58bf4d3406dc4404e29bcb8c89fd22589d57)  BUG=chrome-os-partner:56469 TEST=read i2c hold time register, the value is correct  Change-Id: I1645a5ff2ce5867f907a6fbdd9f5e4d0052f3f4e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/384072 Commit-Ready: Zhuo-hao Lee &lt;zhuo-hao.lee@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Zhuo-hao Lee &lt;zhuo-hao.lee@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="384072" owner_email="zhuo-hao.lee@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/72/384072/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I490f8450b4080ef9ccf5aa0b37b75afa459730bb" commit="2c91592b1e873fb7a4ed4b71846e12595984939e" commit_message="Update target-chromium-os-test ebuild to include contextlib2 and setuptools.  This is needed for running Android WiFi test framework ACTS.  BUG=None TEST=verified with VM test image; both Python packages could be imported  Change-Id: I490f8450b4080ef9ccf5aa0b37b75afa459730bb Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/384029 Commit-Ready: Tien Chang &lt;tienchang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Tien Chang &lt;tienchang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="384029" owner_email="tienchang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/29/384029/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I9854dde6880a789e0acb2b1f6a06b43c73a5a2df" commit="225147ad3800000366e3b0643d2d354d3d188149" commit_message="Cr50: I2CS: Clear IRQ at beginning of ISR  If the host sends a back to back I2CS write followed by a read of the access register, then the read IRQ can be missed by FW because it was clearing this bit at the end of the ISR. This would result in a following write to have the incorrect number of bytes since the address register byte from the read that wasn't processed gets left in the HW write fifo.  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:40397 TEST=manual The issue was happening at the beginning of depthcharge. Without this fix, I would see the Cr50 console message: 'data size mismatch for reg 0x0 rx 2, need 1' After moving the IRQ clear could not reproduce this message. In addition, the debug I2CS log showed that there was a read transaction immediately following the write.  Change-Id: I9854dde6880a789e0acb2b1f6a06b43c73a5a2df Signed-off-by: Scott &lt;scollyer@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/382687 Commit-Ready: Scott Collyer &lt;scollyer@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Scott Collyer &lt;scollyer@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="382687" owner_email="scollyer@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/87/382687/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I8db2d11de7f9586f3e9d19f8706b393f037ccc06" commit="de6277926c1b085d69b665449cf1db79cdf39a42" commit_message="CHROMIUM: sfe: fast_classifier_recv() and other functions can be static  Fix the following build warnings.  drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/sfe/fast-classifier/fast-classifier.c:203:5:  warning: no previous prototype for fast_classifier_recv  drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/sfe/shortcut-fe/sfe_cm.c:124:5:  warning: no previous prototype for sfe_cm_recv  drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/sfe/shortcut-fe/sfe_cm.c:860:5:  warning: no previous prototype for sfe_cm_device_event  BUG=chrome-os-partner:56410 TEST=Build sfe without warnings  Change-Id: I8db2d11de7f9586f3e9d19f8706b393f037ccc06 Signed-off-by: Fengguang Wu &lt;fengguang.wu@intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/384632 Reviewed-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Kishan Kunduru &lt;kkunduru@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Grant Grundler &lt;grundler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="384632" owner_email="groeck@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/32/384632/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I992d96728388437a8c75e07f3c7511f2f7d928ee" commit="ec38d20b17835cfbe89788b79ef60ddc559119f8" commit_message="libchrome.eclass: add cros-debug dependency  This eclass depends on the cros-debug USE flag but does not inherit cros-debug where the dependency on the flag is defined.  This has been working because most packages that use libchrome use platform as well, which inherits the cros-debug eclass.  BUG=none TEST=emerge-$BOARD with package depending on libchrome but not cros-debug  Change-Id: I992d96728388437a8c75e07f3c7511f2f7d928ee Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/384355 Commit-Ready: Aaron Kemp &lt;kemp@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Aaron Kemp &lt;kemp@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="384355" owner_email="kemp@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/55/384355/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="8795.0.0-rc3"/></manifest>